(6802880, 1022016, 84668, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments and votes. For those who are interested this is the bokeh created by some christmas lights that were coming from near my son to my left hand (yes, I put my left hand just on the right side of the camera). I positioned Lucas so the lights would appear going out of his mouth and coming toward the camera. Lighting on Lucas is a single speedlite and a reflector. The title unfortunatelly stayed wrong until the  first 32 votes due to a bug on the site. Then finally they fixed it. The title is a reference to what the wolf says to the pigs before trying to destroy their houses on the 3 pigs fabule. Hence the angry expression of Lucas.<br/>Canon 5d mk Ii<br/>Tamron 90mm f2.8<br/>ISO100<br/>1/160<br/> <br/>Editing was minimal.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-06-27 11:59:49.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments and votes. For those who are interested this is the bokeh created by some christmas lights that were coming from near my son to my left hand (yes, I put my left hand just on the right side of the camera). I positioned Lucas so the lights would appear going out of his mouth and coming toward the camera. Lighting on Lucas is a single speedlite and a reflector. The title unfortunatelly stayed wrong until the  first 32 votes due to a bug on the site. Then finally they fixed it. The title is a reference to what the wolf says to the pigs before trying to destroy their houses on the 3 pigs fabule. Hence the angry expression of Lucas.Canon 5d mk IiTamron 90mm f2.8ISO1001/160 Editing was minimal.', '2012-06-27 09:34:52.000000', '2012-06-27 12:59:49.000000', 0),
(6802907, 1021998, 77196, '<td valign="top">Very nice image, and very interesting voting curve. I think your score suffered from the "not what I expected, and different from all the other entries" syndrome. <br/>The lines are very nice, but for me, it is the bright colors that make the shot (bright, in comparison with each other). Perhaps another way of saying it is that the colors are not all from the same color family, and provide a jumpy feel that contrasts with the smooth lines'' flowing feel.<br/></td>', 'Very nice image, and very interesting voting curve. I think your score suffered from the "not what I expected, and different from all the other entries" syndrome. The lines are very nice, but for me, it is the bright colors that make the shot (bright, in comparison with each other). Perhaps another way of saying it is that the colors are not all from the same color family, and provide a jumpy feel that contrasts with the smooth lines'' flowing feel.', '2012-06-27 10:08:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6802911, 1021773, 77196, '<td valign="top">Not yours, I hope!<br/>Nice leading lines and interesting patterns in the walls. The far window serves as an anchor for the image.</td>', 'Not yours, I hope!Nice leading lines and interesting patterns in the walls. The far window serves as an anchor for the image.', '2012-06-27 10:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6802916, 1021753, 77196, '<td valign="top">Sorry to blow your "no comments" on this shot. It took me a while to figure out what it was - at first it looked like an abstract of the back side of a woman in a pink dress (mid-back down), with her arms hanging at either side. The laser pointer adds an interesting effect.</td>', 'Sorry to blow your "no comments" on this shot. It took me a while to figure out what it was - at first it looked like an abstract of the back side of a woman in a pink dress (mid-back down), with her arms hanging at either side. The laser pointer adds an interesting effect.', '2012-06-27 10:14:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(6802917, 1021833, 144365, '<td valign="top">From now on, I''m going to give photos I like piss poor scores. Of recent, I''m noticing an inverse correlation between photos I like and where they finish. I thought this was one of the better ones in the challenge. Guess I was wrong.</td>', 'From now on, I''m going to give photos I like piss poor scores. Of recent, I''m noticing an inverse correlation between photos I like and where they finish. I thought this was one of the better ones in the challenge. Guess I was wrong.', '2012-06-27 10:18:45.000000', NULL, 0);
